Zero0.12 final ISO verification and current desktop gallery
Date:2026-11-17
Final ISO SHA256: c7e5903efee4b773e3b527168c7a1606fa73be9c99417cf742e3996d58137305

Result: PASS. BIOS64, BIOS32 without long mode/PAE, UEFI64 and UEFI32
again completed40 commands and a cold restart each on the final ISO.
This final160-command run verifies the same Zero/Ezero whole-file APIs,
failure recovery, persistent files/deletion and Ztext decode/rejection cases
as the earlier report.ztext. Earlier280-command filesystem/profile evidence
remains separately identified by its own candidate ISO SHA256.

Current gallery: actual1920x1080 BIOS64 framebuffer, captured from the final
ISO above. The VM used only a new private data disk outside the project.
No kernel changes, mockups, generated artwork or edited screenshot pixels.
- desktop.zpix: initial two-terminal desktop with actual info command output.
- tile.zpix: three live terminals in the native tile layout; Ezero output and
  real create/save/watch/read operations are visible.
- scroll.zpix: the same three terminals in the horizontal strip layout,
  with terminal2 focused and adjacent windows partially visible.

Original zero-picture encoded each external P6 framebuffer capture directly
to ZPIX0001 and verified it. Decoding each image with that same original tool
reproduced the exact P6 file byte-for-byte. Product images use only.zpix;
intermediate PPM files remain outside the project. Native terminal focus can
emit a second serial prompt; the capture harness waits for the command echo
before accepting completion. This required no product change.

All VM processes are stopped. Source kernel is unchanged from the verified
candidate. Tests use QEMU TCG; they do not claim native VirtualBox or PS/2 input
coverage. The screenshots show current output, including current font/layout.

